 {"id":"fabro-febd","title":"qualitygate: fabro-server graph-render tests need target/debug/fabro — gate only builds touched crates and fails 3 tests deterministically","status":"open","type":"bug","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T07:49:03.612Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T07:49:03.612Z","description":"Evidence (develop run 01M1VZTJSZ551NFPHPXD429MG0, tester stage, 2026-09-06): scripts/qualitygate.nu gates only the touched crates, but fabro-server graph-render unit tests (server::tests::get_graph_returns_svg, render_graph_from_manifest_*) invoke target/debug/fabro. When a run touches fabro-server WITHOUT fabro-cli in the touched set, the binary is missing and the gate fails 3 tests deterministically — the 01M1VZTJSZ55 run burned a whole implementer revisit on this. Fix directions: (a) qualitygate builds 'cargo build -p fabro-cli --bin fabro' whenever fabro-server is in the touched set (make the dependency explicit in the gate recipe), or (b) the tests skip with a clear skip message when the binary is absent (worse: hides real regressions), or (c) decouple the tests from the CLI binary via a test-support builder. Prefer (a).","labels":["workflows","revision"]}
 {"id":"fabro-bde4","title":"engine: fabro_run_wait until=merged needs a gate-failure signal — OPEN PR with failed checks must not loop timeouts forever","status":"closed","type":"feature","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T09:42:18.217Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T10:49:42.591Z","description":"Incident 2026-09-07 (conductor pass 01M1XCC9SP1YH38326ZCVJZT3J, develop child 01M1XCHJTDBJKZ31VFMY1KD61Q, PR #33): the develop child merged its work and enabled auto-merge, but the dogfood gate FAILED and a later base push made the PR DIRTY. The conductor leg waits with fabro_run_wait until=merged; ADR-0016 wait results are terminal|merged|closed_unmerged|timeout — a PR that is OPEN with failed checks (or DIRTY) matches NONE of them, so every wait returns timeout and the agent re-waits: 5 chained fabro_run_wait calls over 2+ hours with zero routing until manual repair (debug!-level fix + base merge pushed to the run branch, 09:3x UTC). Wanted: (a) the wait result gains a distinct reached value (e.g. 'blocked' or 'checks_failed') when the linked PR is open but its required checks concluded FAILURE, or its merge state is DIRTY/BLOCKED for a sustained window; (b) conductor prompts route that value to a repair child or park with a clear reason instead of re-waiting; (c) regression test: open PR + failed checks + until=merged returns the new value, not timeout. Related: fabro-94e8 (auto-rebase for stale bases), fabro-6a77 (branch-pushed-PR-failed completion semantics), ADR-0016.","labels":["engine","workflows"],"closedAt":"2026-09-07T10:49:42.591Z"}
 {"id":"fabro-4815","title":"Qualitygate: exit with a status that distinguishes deterministic failures from transient infra","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T11:14:51.580Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T11:14:51.580Z","description":"In scripts/qualitygate.nu, make red exits distinguishable (e.g. a dedicated exit status for deterministic misses vs infra flake) so engine checkpoint classification stops recording deterministic failures as failure_class: \"transient_infra\". Evidence from run 01M1XN2KWG6T0PHRTJWZ8R0AZX: the checkpoint classified the fabro-febd deterministic failure as transient_infra even though the tracker documents it as deterministic. Expected effect: deterministic bugs stop being treated as retryable noise and the Gate-red bounce can prefer known-bug matching over retry. Distinct from open seed fabro-e988, which only prints a critical-first failure summary.\nBasis: run 01M1XN2KWG6T0PHRTJWZ8R0AZX, workflow version 8afe037fc8c61680097f808a27f66ee20da8b546373f6e6e69ad4a09aee94a98, commit 5ff61b59afe4f2afa5fbcf28bb4730bc8ccfb83d","labels":["revision"]}
